//
// New Jersey Gross Income Tax withholding: the Division of Taxation's
// percentage-method Rate Tables A-E (one table per payroll period), with
// allowances from Form NJ-W4.
//
//   taxable = wages - allowances x (allowance value for the period)
//   tax     = base + rate x (taxable - "over") from the selected table, + line 5
//
// Tables were generated by tools/state/generate_nj.py from the Division's
// "Tables for Percentage Method of Withholding" (applicable to wages paid on
// and after October 1, 2020 - still the edition the September 2025 NJ-WT
// links to, so they apply to 2025 and 2026). The PDF has two print defects
// the generator corrects and reports: Rate D quarterly prints "$15.000" for
// $15,000 (the same row's "excess over" column reads $15,000), and Rate C
// semiannual's top rate is set as "1   1.8%" (11.8%, like every other
// table's top bracket - the generator now asserts that for all 40 tables).
// Rows are [overCents, baseCents, rateBasisPoints].
//
// Which table (NJ-WT, "Which Rate Table to Use"; Form NJ-W4 line 2/3):
//   Single or Married/CU partner separate -> Rate A
//   Married/CU couple joint, head of household, qualifying widow(er) -> Rate B
//   ...unless the employee chose a table (A-E) on NJ-W4 line 3.
//
// Wages: New Jersey excludes 401(k) contributions up to the federal limit,
// but taxes contributions to other retirement plans (NJ-WT, "Compensation
// Not Subject to Withholding"). This engine's only deferral is a 401(k)
// within the federal limit, so the base is federal income-tax wages.
//
// No NJ-W4 on file: the current NJ-WT doesn't say. (The 2007 NJ-WT said to
// use the marital status from the federal W-4; today's federal W-4 has no
// allowances.) This withholds at Rate A with zero allowances - the
// higher-withholding choice - and says so (formBasis).
//
// Not covered: the NJ-PA reciprocal agreement (a Pennsylvania resident who
// files Form NJ-165 is not withheld on in NJ), and NJ's unemployment,
// disability and family-leave payroll contributions (not income tax).

